        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "13-GEOPHYSICS - Geophysics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nElastic rebound theory (Reid, 1906):\n  Tectonic stress accumulates in rock → elastic deformation\n  → failure at fault → rapid slip → elastic energy released as seismic waves\n  → surfaces spring back (rebound) from deformed state"
    },
    {
      "id": "13-GEOPHYSICS.md#015",
      "path": [
        "13-GEOPHYSICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:natural-sciences:13-geophysics, git-history:natural-sciences:13-geophysics]",
        "canonical_path": "natural-sciences/13-GEOPHYSICS.md",
        "concepts": "[geophysics]",
        "current_path": "natural-sciences/13-GEOPHYSICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:natural-sciences:geophysics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "natural-sciences",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geophysics]",
        "section": "natural-sciences",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "13-GEOPHYSICS - Geophysics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Fault types:\n  Normal fault:   hanging wall moves DOWN (extensional, divergent margins)\n  Reverse fault:  hanging wall moves UP (compressional, subduction zones)\n  Strike-slip:    horizontal motion along fault (transform margins; San Andreas, NAF)\n  Thrust:         low-angle reverse fault → mountain building"
    },
    {
      "id": "13-GEOPHYSICS.md#016",
      "path": [
        "13-GEOPHYSICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:natural-sciences:13-geophysics, git-history:natural-sciences:13-geophysics]",
        "canonical_path": "natural-sciences/13-GEOPHYSICS.md",
        "concepts": "[geophysics]",
        "current_path": "natural-sciences/13-GEOPHYSICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:natural-sciences:geophysics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "natural-sciences",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geophysics]",
        "section": "natural-sciences",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "13-GEOPHYSICS - Geophysics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Seismic moment: M₀ = μ · A · D\n  μ = shear modulus (~3 × 10¹⁰ Pa), A = fault area, D = average slip\n  Moment magnitude: Mw = (2/3) log₁₀(M₀) − 6.0\n  Each unit increase: 31.6× more energy, 10× more ground motion amplitude\n```"
    },
