      "text": "### Seismic Waves"
    },
    {
      "id": "13-GEOPHYSICS.md#018",
      "path": [
        "13-GEOPHYSICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:natural-sciences:13-geophysics, git-history:natural-sciences:13-geophysics]",
        "canonical_path": "natural-sciences/13-GEOPHYSICS.md",
        "concepts": "[geophysics]",
        "current_path": "natural-sciences/13-GEOPHYSICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:natural-sciences:geophysics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "natural-sciences",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geophysics]",
        "section": "natural-sciences",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "13-GEOPHYSICS - Geophysics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nBody waves (travel through interior):\n  P-waves: compressional; vₚ = √((K + 4/3·G)/ρ)   ~6–8 km/s in crust\n  S-waves: shear; vₛ = √(G/ρ)                      ~3.5–4.5 km/s in crust\n  vₚ/vₛ ≈ √3 for typical crustal rock (Poisson ratio ~0.25)"
    },
